  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 21 May 1958 and counted in the Town Hall on Thursday 22 May: three aldermen (for six years) and twelve councillors, twenty-four candidates. Labels as printed: U Unionist, L Labour (Northern Ireland Labour Party), R Portadown Rent and Ratepayers' Association. The Portadown News prints surnames only; initials and the outgoing members (asterisked) are from the Northern Whig. Electorate 9,002; votes cast 5,401 (59.88 per cent). Aldermen: two Unionists and one Rent and Ratepayers' Association candidate were elected; H. R. O'Lone, ex-Mayor, was defeated; 380 spoilt aldermanic papers."
